              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety"} variety
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+characteristic"} positive characteristic
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
            attached to it, called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em Artin-Mazur formal group
          %p
            The Artin-Mazur formal group in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
            version of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+infinity-group"} Picard n-group
            of flat/holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles"} circle n-bundles
            on the given variety. Therefore for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            one also speaks of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+Picard+group"} formal Picard group
            and for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+Brauer+group"} formal Brauer group
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#deformations_of_higher_line_bundles_of_cohomology
            Deformations of higher line bundles (of
            = succeed "-cohomology)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(-,\mathbb{G}_m)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+scheme"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+scheme"} proper
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variety"} variety
            over an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            Writing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_m
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{et}^\bullet(-,-)
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/etale+cohomology"} etale cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{et}^n(X,\mathbb{G}_m)
            classifies
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_m
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundle"} principal n-bundles
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+n-bundles"}> line n-bundles
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+2-gerbe"} bundle (n-1)-gerbes
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a{:href => "Brauer%20group#RelationToEtaleCohomology"} Brauer group – relation to étale cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+group"} Picard group
            while for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            this contains (as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion subgroup
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Accordingly, for each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+algebra"} Artin algebra
            regarded as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+point"} infinitesimally thickened point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ArtAlg
                    %mi k
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in ArtAlg_k^{op}
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{et}^n(X\times_{Spec(k)} S,\mathbb{G}_m)
            is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundle"} principal n-bundles
            on a formal thickening of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The defining inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to S
            of the unique global point induces a restriction map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spec
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msubsup
                    %mi H
                    %mi et
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n_{et}(X\times_{Spec(k)} S, \mathbb{G}_m)\to H^n_{et}(X, \mathbb{G}_m))
            which restricts an
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            itself. The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            of this map hence may be thought of as the group of
            = succeed "-parameterized" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformations"} deformations
            of the trivial
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_m
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            (For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            this is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+neighbourhood"} infinitesimal neighbourhood
            of the neutral element in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+scheme"} Picard scheme
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Pic
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pic_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            one will need to genuinely speak about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+stacks"} Picard stacks
            and higher stacks.)
          %p
            As
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            varies, these groups of deformations naturally form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            on “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimally+thickened+points"}> infinitesimally thickened points
            ” (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isbell+duality"} formal duals
            to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin+algebras"} Artin algebras
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
              as above, write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi ArtAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo →
                    %mi Grp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Phi_X^n \;\colon\; ArtAlg_k \to Grp
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spec
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi S
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Phi_X^n(S) \coloneqq \mathrm{ker}(H^n_{et}(X\times_{Spec(k)} S, \mathbb{G}_m)\to H^n_{et}(X, \mathbb{G}_m))
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur77"}> Artin-Mazur 77, II.1 “Main examples”
            )
          %p
            The fundamental result of (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur77"}> Artin-Mazur 77, II
            ) is that under the above hypotheses this presheaf is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prorepresentable+functor"} pro-representable
            by a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_X^n
            %strong Artin-Mazur formal group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p More in detail:
          #SufficientConditionsForRepresentability.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+morphism"} proper
              over an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraically+closed+field"} algebraically closed field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            %p
              A sufficient condition for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_X^k
              to be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prorepresentable+functor"} pro-representable
              by a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
              is that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_X^{k-1}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formally smooth
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim H^{k-1}(X,\mathcal{O}_X) = 0
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^{k-1}(X)
              vanishes, hence is trivially formally smooth, hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^k(X)
              is representable
          %p
            The first statement appears as (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur77"}> Artin-Mazur 77, corollary (2.12)
            ). The second as (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur77"}> Artin-Mazur 77, corollary (4.2)
            ).
          #Dimension.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^k_X
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi X
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi dim
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dim(\Phi^k_X) = dim H^k(X,\mathcal{O}_X)
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur77"}> Artin-Mazur 77, II.4
            ).
          %h3#DeformationsOfDeligneCohomology Deformations of higher line bundles with connection (of Deligne cohomology)
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#ArtinMazur77"}> Artin-Mazur 77, section III
            ) is also discussed the formal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+n-bundles+with+connection"} line n-bundles with connection
            (classified by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Deligne+complex"} Deligne complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group"} formal group
          %p
            Notice that by the discussion at
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/intermediate%20Jacobian#CharacterizationAsHodgeTrivialDeligneCohomology"} intermediate Jacobian – Characterization as Hodge-trivial Deligne cohomology
            the formal deformation theory of Deligne cohomology yields the formal completion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobians"} intermediate Jacobians
            (all in suitable degree).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#general General
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  For a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curve"} curve
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
